以下是一个用 C 语言编写的简单的九九乘法表程序：

c

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int i, j;

    for (i = 1; i <= 9; i++) {
        for (j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
            printf("%d x %d = %d\t", j, i, i*j);
        }
        printf("\n");
    }

    return 0;
}

这个程序使用了两个嵌套的 for 循环来打印九九乘法表。外层循环变量 i 用于控制行数，内层循环变量 j 用于控制列数。每一行从 1 开始，直到该行数为止，打印该行中每个数和该行数的乘积，并在数之间添加制表符 \t 以便对齐。

这个程序输出的结果如下：

1 x 1 = 1	
1 x 2 = 2	2 x 2 = 4	
1 x 3 = 3	2 x 3 = 6	3 x 3 = 9	
1 x 4 = 4	2 x 4 = 8	3 x 4 = 12	4 x 4 = 16	
1 x 5 = 5	2 x 5 = 10	3 x 5 = 15	4 x 5 = 20	5 x 5 = 25	
1 x 6 = 6	2 x 6 = 12	3 x 6 = 18	4 x 6 = 24	5 x 6 = 30	6 x 6 = 36	
1 x 7 = 7	2 x 7 = 14	3 x 7 = 21	4 x 7 = 28	5 x 7 = 35	6 x 7 = 42	7 x 7 = 49	
1 x 8 = 8	2 x 8 = 16	3 x 8 = 24	4 x 8 = 32	5 x 8 = 40	6 x 8 = 48	7 x 8 = 56	8 x 8 = 64	
1 x 9 = 9	2 x 9 = 18	3 x 9 = 27	4 x 9 = 36	5 x 9 = 45	6 x 9 = 54	7 x 9 = 63	8 x 9 = 72	9 x 9 = 81

Un exemple d'un codi en C++ per sumar dos valors sencers i després mostrar-los en la terminal.

#include <iostream>

int main() {
  // Declaració de les variables
  int a, b;
  int suma;

  // Demanar les dades d'entrada a l'usuari
  std::cout << "Introdueix el primer nombre: ";
  std::cin >> a;
  std::cout << "Introdueix el segon nombre: ";
  std::cin >> b;

  // Càlcul de la suma
  suma = a + b;

  // Impressió del resultat a la terminal
  std::cout << "La suma de " << a << " i " << b << " és " << suma << std::endl;

  return 0;
}

The singularity probability \(p_n\) for an \(n \times n\) matrix with entries chosen independently and uniformly from \(\{-1, 1\}\) is asymptotically equivalent to \(\binom{n}{2} 2^{1-n}\) as \(n \to \infty\).

This asymptotic equivalent arises because the dominant contribution to singularity comes from the event that at least one pair of rows is parallel (i.e., identical or negatives of each other). The probability that a specific pair of rows is parallel is \(2 \cdot (1/2)^n = 2^{1-n}\). There are \(\binom{n}{2}\) such pairs, and for large \(n\), the inclusion-exclusion principle shows that the first term \(\binom{n}{2} 2^{1-n}\) dominates, with higher-order terms decaying faster. Thus, \(p_n \sim \binom{n}{2} 2^{1-n}\).

\boxed{\binom{n}{2} \cdot 2^{1-n}}

